IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cus-traveller`

-- Customs Act 1960, ss 19, 20, 93, 109, 110, 115, 115A, 119, 124, 126, 127, 128 to 128L, 129 and 136 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_customs-act-1960_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a traveller within the allowance` MEANS Arrival WITH
    `I carry dutiable goods beyond my duty free allowance` IS FALSE
    `I carry dutiable goods for which no allowance is granted` IS FALSE
    `the point of entry has a Red Channel and a Green Channel` IS TRUE
    `I paid the duty before I proceeded` IS FALSE
    `I went through the Green Channel` IS TRUE

`a traveller with excess liquor in the Green Channel` MEANS Arrival WITH
    `I carry dutiable goods beyond my duty free allowance` IS TRUE
    `I carry dutiable goods for which no allowance is granted` IS FALSE
    `the point of entry has a Red Channel and a Green Channel` IS TRUE
    `I paid the duty before I proceeded` IS FALSE
    `I went through the Green Channel` IS TRUE

`a traveller who declares at the Red Channel and pays` MEANS Arrival WITH
    `I carry dutiable goods beyond my duty free allowance` IS TRUE
    `I carry dutiable goods for which no allowance is granted` IS FALSE
    `the point of entry has a Red Channel and a Green Channel` IS TRUE
    `I paid the duty before I proceeded` IS TRUE
    `I went through the Green Channel` IS FALSE

`a traveller at a land checkpoint with no channels, who declares but does not pay` MEANS Arrival WITH
    `I carry dutiable goods beyond my duty free allowance` IS FALSE
    `I carry dutiable goods for which no allowance is granted` IS TRUE
    `the point of entry has a Red Channel and a Green Channel` IS FALSE
    `I paid the duty before I proceeded` IS FALSE
    `I went through the Green Channel` IS FALSE

`a woman searched by a woman, nothing asked` MEANS `My search` WITH
