`the owner of a car lent to a smuggler` MEANS Find WITH
    `I had the thing containing the goods` IS FALSE
    `I had the keys of the thing containing the goods` IS FALSE
    `I had the keys of the premises where the goods were found` IS FALSE
    `I had a document of title to the goods` IS FALSE
    `the goods were found in a vehicle` IS TRUE
    `I own the vehicle or have it on hire-purchase` IS TRUE
    `I was in charge of the vehicle at the time` IS FALSE

`a passenger in the car` MEANS Find WITH
    `I had the thing containing the goods` IS FALSE
    `I had the keys of the thing containing the goods` IS FALSE
    `I had the keys of the premises where the goods were found` IS FALSE
    `I had a document of title to the goods` IS FALSE
    `the goods were found in a vehicle` IS TRUE
    `I own the vehicle or have it on hire-purchase` IS FALSE
    `I was in charge of the vehicle at the time` IS FALSE

`an owner who lent the car without due care` MEANS `My vehicle` WITH
    `I am the owner` IS TRUE
    `I had hired it out to someone else` IS FALSE
    `I am the hirer` IS FALSE
    `I used it, or let someone use it, to keep or carry the goods` IS TRUE
    `the goods are specified goods` IS TRUE
    `I exercised due care to find out they were not` IS FALSE

`an owner who had hired the car out to a hirer` MEANS `My vehicle` WITH
    `I am the owner` IS TRUE
    `I had hired it out to someone else` IS TRUE
    `I am the hirer` IS FALSE
    `I used it, or let someone use it, to keep or carry the goods` IS TRUE
    `the goods are specified goods` IS TRUE
    `I exercised due care to find out they were not` IS FALSE

`a written demand in year 4 that states the amount` MEANS Demand WITH
    `it is in writing` IS TRUE
    `the date I paid the duty` IS (Date 1 3 2021)
    `the date of the demand` IS (Date 1 3 2025)
    `it states the amount or the circumstances` IS TRUE
    `the short levy came from my fraud or evasion` IS FALSE

`a written demand in year 7 after my evasion` MEANS Demand WITH
    `it is in writing` IS TRUE
    `the date I paid the duty` IS (Date 1 3 2019)
    `the date of the demand` IS (Date 1 3 2026)
    `it states the amount or the circumstances` IS TRUE
    `the short levy came from my fraud or evasion` IS TRUE

`a half tank past the gantry` MEANS Departure WITH
    `the vehicle is registered under the Road Traffic Act 1961` IS TRUE
    `I am in charge of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `I left or tried to leave Singapore in it` IS FALSE
    `I drove past the Customs gantry before the departure bay` IS TRUE
    `I proved I was not trying to leave` IS FALSE
    `the fuel in the tank` IS 0.5
    `the minimum the Minister's order prescribes` IS 0.75
    `I had written permission before I tried to leave` IS FALSE

`a half tank with permission given beforehand` MEANS Departure WITH
    `the vehicle is registered under the Road Traffic Act 1961` IS TRUE
    `I am in charge of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `I left or tried to leave Singapore in it` IS FALSE
    `I drove past the Customs gantry before the departure bay` IS TRUE
    `I proved I was not trying to leave` IS FALSE
    `the fuel in the tank` IS 0.5
    `the minimum the Minister's order prescribes` IS 0.75
    `I had written permission before I tried to leave` IS TRUE

§ `s 93 -- declaring at the border`

#ASSERT NOT `Must I declare and pay duty before I proceed` `a traveller within the allowance`
#ASSERT `Must I declare and pay duty before I proceed` `a traveller with excess liquor in the Green Channel`

#ASSERT `Where must I declare` `a traveller who declares at the Red Channel and pays` EQUALS `at the Red Channel`
#ASSERT `Where must I declare` `a traveller at a land checkpoint with no channels, who declares but does not pay` EQUALS `to the proper officer of customs at the customs station`

#ASSERT NOT `Are my goods deemed uncustomed` `a traveller who declares at the Red Channel and pays`
#ASSERT `Are my goods deemed uncustomed` `a traveller at a land checkpoint with no channels, who declares but does not pay`

#ASSERT `Am I presumed to possess uncustomed goods because I took the Green Channel` `a traveller with excess liquor in the Green Channel`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I presumed to possess uncustomed goods because I took the Green Channel` `a traveller within the allowance`

#TRACE `my duty at the customs station` `a traveller who declares at the Red Channel and pays` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the traveller` DOES `declare the goods and pay the duty` AT 0

§ `ss 109, 129 -- search and questions`

#ASSERT `May my person be searched now` `a woman searched by a woman, nothing asked`
#ASSERT NOT `May my person be searched now` `a man who asked for a senior officer, before one arrives`
#ASSERT NOT `May my person be searched now` `a woman about to be searched by a man`

#ASSERT NOT `May my baggage be searched now` `a traveller who asked to watch the baggage search and came back in time, now absent`

#ASSERT `Must I answer the officer's question` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I answer the officer's question` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 128 to 128KA, 129, 136 -- the offences`

#ASSERT `Which section makes what I did an offence` `giving away my duty free allowance goods to someone in Singapore` EQUALS `section 128J`
#ASSERT `Which section makes what I did an offence` `failing to declare dutiable goods I bring in` EQUALS `section 128B`
#ASSERT `Which section makes what I did an offence` `letting someone use my vehicle to carry smuggled goods, without due care` EQUALS `section 128KA`
#ASSERT `Which section makes what I did an offence` `consuming my own duty free allowance` EQUALS `no offence under this Act`

#ASSERT `Is it a specified offence` `section 128J`
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a specified offence` `section 128B`
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a specified offence` `section 128KA`

#ASSERT `Can I say I did not mean it or did not know` `section 128B` EQUALS `nothing: the Act says inadvertence or lack of intent is no defence`
#ASSERT `Can I say I did not mean it or did not know` `section 128KA` EQUALS `that I exercised due care to find out what the goods were`

§ `s 128L and the other penalties`

#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `$40 of duty on wine I gave away` EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `$10 of duty on a pack of cigarettes in my pocket` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `$2,000 of duty on 5 kg of tobacco` EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `$2,000 of duty on 5 kg of tobacco, after an earlier 3 kg tobacco conviction` EQUALS JUST 60000
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `wine given away whose duty cannot be ascertained` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined` `5 kg of tobacco whose duty cannot be ascertained` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `$40 of duty on wine I gave away` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `$1,000 of duty on spirits I denied having` EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `$2,000 of duty on 5 kg of tobacco` EQUALS JUST 40000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `wine given away whose duty cannot be ascertained` EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `an untrue declaration with $25,000 of duty payable` EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `leaving with a near-empty tank` EQUALS JUST 500

#ASSERT `For how many months at most can I be imprisoned` `$40 of duty on wine I gave away` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `For how many months at most can I be imprisoned` `$300 of duty on wine sold, after an earlier non-tobacco conviction` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `For how many months at most can I be imprisoned` `$2,000 of duty on 5 kg of tobacco` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `For how many months at most can I be imprisoned` `$100 of duty on cigarettes, after an earlier cigarette conviction` EQUALS 72

#ASSERT `Must the court both fine and imprison me` `$2,000 of duty on 5 kg of tobacco, after an earlier 3 kg tobacco conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `Must the court both fine and imprison me` `$100 of duty on cigarettes, after an earlier cigarette conviction`

§ `ss 115, 115A, 128L(6) -- presumptions`

#ASSERT `Am I presumed to possess the goods until I prove otherwise` `the owner of a car lent to a smuggler`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I presumed to possess the goods until I prove otherwise` `a passenger in the car`

#ASSERT `Must I prove it` `where the goods came from`

#ASSERT `Am I deemed to have known what the goods were` `section 128E` FALSE

